          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Heisenberg group
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em Weyl-Heisenberg group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} integrating
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
          %p There are several such, and so the conventions in the literature vary slightly as to which one to pick by default.
          %p
            The Heisenberg group historically originates in and still has its strongest ties to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
            acting on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states"} space of states
            induced from those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            on a linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            – which are given by linear or by constant functions. So any Heisenberg group is a subgroup of a group of observables in certain simple examples of quantum mechanical systems.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Heisenberg group
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
          %p We spell out some special cases in detail.
          %h3#H3InComponents
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            in components
          %p
            The simplest non-trivial example of a Heisenberg group is the unique
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            Lie integration of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi dq
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heis(\mathbb{R}^2, \omega = d p \wedge dq)
            on the the canonical 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            with canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,q)
          %p
            This Heisenberg Lie algebra is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
            from 3 elements, here to be denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{p}, \mathbf{q},\mathbf{e}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\mathbf{q}, \mathbf{p}] = \mathbf{e}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding Heisenberg group is usually denoted
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi exp
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi d
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_3 \coloneqq \exp Heis(\mathbb{R}^2 , d p \wedge d q)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{a,b,c}
                  \=
                  \\exp(a \mathbf{q} + b \mathbf{p} )\exp(c \mathbf{e})
          %p
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b , c\in \mathbb{R}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff+formula"} Baker-Campbell-Hausdorff formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi e
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(a_1 \mathbf{q} + b_1 \mathbf{p})
                  \\exp(c_1 \mathbf{e})
                  \\cdot
                  \\exp(a_2 \mathbf{q} + b_2 \mathbf{p})
                  \\exp(c_2 \mathbf{e})
                  \=
                  \\exp\big(
                  (a_1 + b_1) \mathbf{q} + (b_1 + c_1) \mathbf{p}
                  \\big)
                  \\exp\big(
                  c_1 + c_2 - \tfrac{1}{2}(a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1) \mathbf{e}
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            A discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
            of this,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} integrating
            the same
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2 \times U(1)
            (the second factor being the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coprojection"} coprojection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{R}^2 \times \mathbb{R}
                  \\to
                  \\mathbb{R}^2 \times U(1)
          %p
            that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1) \simeq \mathbb{R} / \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            If the circle group is instead thought of as the unit circle in the complex plane, then this quotient is thought of as the exponential map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(2 \pi i (-)) : \mathbb{R} \to U(1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{a, b, c}
                  \=
                  \\exp(a \mathbf{q} + b \mathbf{p} )\exp(2 \pi i c )
          %p and their product is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(a_1 \mathbf{q} + b_1 \mathbf{p})
                  \\exp(2 \pi i c_1 )
                  \\cdot
                  \\exp(a_2 \mathbf{q} + b_2 \mathbf{p})
                  \\exp(2 \pi i c_2 )
                  \=
                  \\exp\big(
                  (a_1 + b_1) \mathbf{q} + (b_1 + c_1) \mathbf{p}
                  \\big)
                  \\exp\Big(
                  2 \pi \mathrm{i}\big(
                  c_1 + c_2 - \tfrac{1}{2}(a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1)
                  \\big)
                  \\Big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            While the Lie algebra is still the same real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            as before, it is now suggestive to write the Lie bracket as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [q,p] = \mathrm{i}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the way the relation appears in texts on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
          %h3#for_a_symplectic_vector_space For a symplectic vector space
          %p
            Generally, there is a Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(V, \omega)
            associated to any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, \omega)
          %p
            Regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            structure underlying its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            structure.
          %p
            The Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(V,\omega)
            is the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \times U(1)
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (v_1, c_1) \cdot (v_2, c_2)
                  \=
                  \\Big(
                  v_1 + v_2, c_1 c_2 \exp\big(2 \pi i \omega(v,w)\big)
                  \\Big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToPoissonBracket Relation to Poisson algebra
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, \omega)
            is in particular a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(V)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+algebra"} Poisson algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            underlying the Poisson algebra contains the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            as the subspace with is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mo *
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^* \hookrightarrow C^\infty(V)
            and the constant functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \hookrightarrow C^\infty(V)
          %p
            For more details in this at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Heisenberg+Lie+algebra#RelationToPoissonAlgebra"} Relation to Poisson algebra
          %h3#RelationToSymplectomorphisms Relation to symplectomorphisms
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToPoissonBracket"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the group that integrates the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
            of the group of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphisms"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphisms
          %p
            (Of course, on a contractible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            such as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphism"} symplectomorphism
            is automatically a
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+symplectomorphism"} Hamiltonian symplectomorphism
          %h3#cocycle_and_extension Cocycle and extension
          %p
            The additive group on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            with group operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (a,b) + (a',b') = (a + a' , b + b')
          %p
            carries a degree=2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cocycle"} group cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\omega \colon
                  \\big((a_1,b_1), (a_2,b_2)\big)
                  \\mapsto
                  a_1 \cdot b_2
                  \\,.
          %p The cocycle condition for this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a_1 \cdot (b_2 + b_3) + a_2 \cdot b_3
                  \=
                  a_1 \cdot b_2 + (a_1 + a_2) \cdot b_3
                  \\,,
          %p
            which evidently holds due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity"} distributivity
          %p
            The Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %a{:href => "group+extension#CentralExtensionClassificationByGroupCohomology"} classified by
            this cocycle.
          %h3#unitary_representations Unitary representations
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone-von+Neumann+theorem"} Stone-von Neumann theorem
          %h3#automorphism_group Automorphism group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the Heisenberg group is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer+Heisenberg+group"} integer Heisenberg group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+CR+manifold"} spherical CR manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+n-group"} Heisenberg n-group
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p An original account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertram+Kostant"}> Bertram Kostant
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization and unitary representations
              = succeed "." do
                %em Lectures in modern analysis and applications III
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 170
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0079068"} doi:10.1007/BFb0079068
          %p
            Review in the context of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone-von+Neumann+theorem"} Stone-von Neumann theorem
          %ul
            %li#Rosenberg2004
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"}> Jonathan Rosenberg
              , p. 7 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Selective History of the Stone-von Neumann Theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %em Operator Algebras, Quantization, and Noncommutative Geometry: A Centennial Celebration Honoring John von Neumann and Marshall H. Stone
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 365
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/conm/365"} doi:10.1090/conm/365
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.umd.edu/~jmr/StoneVNart.pdf"} pdf
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li#PressleySegal
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Pressley"}> Andrew Pressley
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Loop groups
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/loop-groups-9780198535614"} ISBN:9780198535614
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in the context of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+groups"} loop groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernst+Binz"}> Ernst Binz
                , Sonja Pods,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of Heisenberg groups — With Applications in Signal Theory, Optics, Quantization, and Field Quantization
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 151
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-151"} ams:surv-151
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
                , section II.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780817647308"} doi:10.1007/978-0-8176-4731-5
            %li#Woodhouse
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Woodhouse"}> Nicholas Woodhouse
                , pp 166 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric Quantization
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/geometric-quantization-9780198502708"} ISBN:9780198502708
            %li
              %p
                %em Geometric quantization II, Prequantization and the Heisenberg group
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jthomas7/GeomQuant/Lecture2.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of the infinite-dimensional Heisenberg group is in
          %ul
            %li
              Günther Hörmann,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representations of the infinite dimensional Heisenberg group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~michor/hoermann_diss.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+algebras"} group algebras
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+groups"} Heisenberg groups
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+deformation+quantizations"} strict deformation quantizations
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+manifold"} pre-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+spaces"} symplectic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+field+of+C-star+algebras"} continuous fields of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+algebras"} Weyl algebras
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernst+Binz"}> Ernst Binz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reinhard+Honegger"} Reinhard Honegger
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Rieckers"} Alfred Rieckers
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Infinite dimensional Heisenberg group algebra and field-theoretic strict deformation quantization
                %strong 38
                1 (2007) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://ijpam.eu/contents/2007-38-1/6/index.html"}> ijpam:2007-38-1/6
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ijpam.eu/contents/2007-38-1/6/6.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reinhard+Honegger"}> Reinhard Honegger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Rieckers"} Alfred Rieckers
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Heisenberg Group Algebra and Strict Weyl Quantization
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Photons in Fock Space and Beyond, Volume I: From Classical to Quantized Radiation Systems
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814696586_0023"} doi;10.1142/9789814696586_0023
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9251-vol1"} doi:10.1142/9251-vol1
          %h3#for_abelian_chernsimons_theory For abelian Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer+Heisenberg+group"} integer Heisenberg group
            describing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+Chern-Simons+theory"} abelian Chern-Simons theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
            (and its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skein+relations"} skein relations
            and
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
          %ul
            %li#GelcaUribe10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R%C4%83zvan+Gelca"}> Răzvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From classical theta functions to topological quantum field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Influence of Solomon Lefschetz in Geometry and Topology: 50 Years of Mathematics at CINVESTAV
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 621
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.3252"} arXiv:1006.3252
                = succeed "," do
